Subject: [PATCH] Makefile: exit, don't return, from filechk_timestamp.h

filechk_timestamp.h's shell script runs as a Makefile recipe line, not
inside a shell function, so `return` outside a function makes dash
(NixOS's /bin/sh) fail the build with "return: can only `return' from
a function or sourced script". Use `exit` instead, which works the
same way here since this is the last command run by the subshell.

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -2330,5 +2330,5 @@
 			LC_ALL=C $${DATE} -u -d "$${SOURCE_DATE}" +'#define U_BOOT_EPOCH %s'; \
 		else \
-			return 42; \
+			exit 42; \
 		fi; \
 	else \
